From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Bowyer <peter@mapledesign.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fellow_logwatcher: skip close flush after shutdown

Storage warn-close already asks the logwatcher to stop scheduling new rewrite
work and performs a normal log flush before shutdown continues. That flush could
return early when the logbuffer only had an active block, so the watcher thread
still performed the only durable active-block/header publication via final
`LBUF_FLUSH_CLOSE` while `fellow_logwatcher_fini()` was waiting in
`pthread_join()`. Large stop-after-purge runs could spend the manager's entire
child-stop grace period in that close-time logbuffer drain and be killed by
vinyltest.

Include active log blocks in `fellow_log_flush()`, so warn-close publishes them
before it marks the watcher as shutting down. Once that shutdown mark is set, do
not start an additional close flush from the watcher exit path. Abandon the
remaining in-memory open logbuffer state and finalize the logbuffer instead.
This still waits for already submitted flush-finish work and outstanding IO
needed for safe ownership teardown, but avoids adding new close-time
active-block/header drain work after the child is already stopping.
---
 src/fellow_log.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/fellow_log.c b/src/fellow_log.c
index e1d013f..9eb9c9b 100644
--- a/src/fellow_log.c
+++ b/src/fellow_log.c
@@ -6593,7 +6593,10 @@ fellow_log_flush(struct fellow_fd *ffd)
 
 	// racy
 	lbuf = ffd->logbuf;
-	if (lbuf->n == 0 && lbuf->regions_to_free == NULL)
+	if (lbuf->n == 0 &&
+	    (lbuf->active.block == NULL ||
+	    lbuf->active.block->nentries == 0) &&
+	    lbuf->regions_to_free == NULL)
 		return;
 
 	lbuf = NULL;
@@ -6649,7 +6649,11 @@ fellow_logwatcher_thread(void *priv)
 	 */
 	assert(ffd->logbuf->state == LBUF_OPEN ||
 	    ffd->logbuf->state == LBUF_PEND);
-	logbuffer_flush(ffd, ffd->logbuf, LBUF_FLUSH_CLOSE, LBUF_ALL);
+	if (ffd->watcher_shutdown)
+		logbuffer_abandon(ffd->logbuf);
+	else
+		logbuffer_flush(ffd, ffd->logbuf, LBUF_FLUSH_CLOSE,
+		    LBUF_ALL);
 	ffd->logbuf->state = LBUF_FINI;
 	logbuffer_fini(ffd->logbuf);
 
